The release PR is up as #74: https://github.com/softwarewrighter/reva-fork/pull/74. Its full gate passed; the only failure was the known `docs-samples` on macOS. I reran the goldens on sed-rs 0.3.0 with the same result.

After you merge #74, I'll:
1. merge `dev` into `main`;
2. publish the live demo with `scripts/publish-pages.sh`, which builds from `main`;
3. check in Chrome that the live demo serves 2026.1101.1;
4. complete step 39 and return to step 40 (`local-image-everywhere`).

**Step 40 is paused but already diagnosed.** A CoSy image doesn't resume because of how strings compiled into words are saved, not because of anything specific to CoSy:
- Forth's `save NAME` updates a length before saving, so its images work.
- The CLI's `--save-image` doesn't, so every string compiled after boot comes back cut off. That includes any `."` in your own words.

The fix goes in when step 40 resumes. The live demo isn't affected: it never uses `--save-image`.

